<article class="env-remark" id="023O">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/023O">Remark <span data-tag="023O">35.3.10</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $f_1, \ldots , f_ n\in R$ generate the unit ideal. The ring $A = \prod _ i R_{f_ i}$ is a faithfully flat $R$-algebra. We remark that the cosimplicial ring $(A/R)_\bullet $ has the following ring in degree $n$: </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \prod \nolimits _{i_0, \ldots , i_ n} R_{f_{i_0}\ldots f_{i_ n}}  \]
</div>
  <p> Hence the results above recover Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/00EJ" data-tag="00EJ">10.24.2</a>, <a href="/tag/00EK" data-tag="00EK">10.24.1</a> and <a href="/tag/00EQ" data-tag="00EQ">10.24.5</a>. But the results above actually say more because of exactness in higher degrees. Namely, it implies that Čech cohomology of quasi-coherent sheaves on affines is trivial. Thus we get a second proof of Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01X9" data-tag="01X9">30.2.1</a>. </p>
</article>